# Security

- Oracle access is read-only. Application SQL lives in the fixed query catalog and uses bind variables.
- Never execute SQL or PL/SQL supplied by a model or by an end user.
- Do not log credentials, DSNs, access tokens, or package source.
- LLM egress stays disabled unless `OIA_LLM_EGRESS_ENABLED` is explicitly set for an approved endpoint.
- Development sign-in is a local access token. It is not a substitute for enterprise SSO.
- Keep `runs/` out of git. Run identifiers must not allow path traversal.
